@Plumy.Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7062

# Every endpoint requires an Entra access token with the access_as_user scope (401 without it).
# Until the Angular login exists, copy one from the browser's dev tools (Authorization header of an /api call).
@token = paste-an-access-token-here

### Create a client company (201 + Location header)
# @name create
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme S.L.",
  "taxId": "b-1234567.4"
}

### Get it back using the Id from the previous response
GET {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Same tax ID again → 409 Conflict
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Duplicate S.L.",
  "taxId": "B12345674"
}

### Invalid tax ID → 400 ProblemDetails
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad S.L.",
  "taxId": "B12345670"
}

### Unknown Id → 404
GET {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{$random.uuid}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Rename (only the name is editable; the tax ID is immutable)
PUT {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Global S.A."
}

### Archive (soft delete) → 204; a second call or a GET afterwards → 404
DELETE {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invitations (firm owner only). Inviting the same address again renews its open invitation
# @name invite
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/firm/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "luis@example.com"
}

### The firm's open invitations, including expired ones
GET {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/firm/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Revoke → 204; a second call → 404
DELETE {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/firm/invitations/{{invite.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Accept, as the invited user (a token for the invited address, with no firm yet). See /api/me → invitations
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/invitations/{{invite.response.body.id}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
